{"id":"pattern-example-001","type":"pattern","fact":"Example: Use mock factories for all test data instead of manual mock objects with 'as Type' assertions.","recommendation":"Create centralized mock factory functions (createMockUser, createMockOrg, etc.) and import them in tests.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"documentation","reference":"Testing guide","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["testing","mocks","factories"],"affectedFiles":["**/*.test.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-os-stderr-merge-001","type":"pattern","fact":"For Pipe-kind subprocess backends, merge stderr into stdout at the OS level by creating ONE pipe via PosixIO.createPipe and using setStdout (useHandleOpen writeH) . setStderr (useHandleOpen writeH) on the SAME write-handle. Two pipes + a user-space accumulator race-interleaves cross-stream bytes inside a chunk; OS-level merge avoids it.","recommendation":"Use this exact pattern in any new Pipe-kind backend factory. The write-end must be hClose'd by the parent after spawn so the reader sees EOF when the child exits. See src/PureClaw/Backend/Local.hs and src/PureClaw/Backend/SSH.hs for the canonical implementation.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"WU8 adversarial review","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["subprocess","ipc","backend","correctness"],"affectedFiles":["src/PureClaw/Backend/Local.hs","src/PureClaw/Backend/SSH.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-concurrent-use-guard-001","type":"pattern","fact":"BackendHandle's documented contract forbids concurrent _bh_send/_bh_recv from multiple threads. The wrapper withConcurrentUseGuard :: BackendHandle -> IO BackendHandle gates both actions on an MVar; second-entrant throws BackendException with BcConcurrentUse. Applied at every successful return from SSH and Tmux factories.","recommendation":"Apply withConcurrentUseGuard to every BackendHandle a new factory returns. The wrapper is a post-construction step (it does NOT belong inside mkDrainerBackendHandle). Tests for the contract live in Backend/SSHSpec.hs under 'WU9.5 disconnect-mid-recv and concurrent-use'.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"WU9.5 implementation","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["concurrency","backend","contract"],"affectedFiles":["src/PureClaw/Handles/Backend.hs","src/PureClaw/Backend/SSH.hs","src/PureClaw/Backend/Tmux.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-tmux-pin-resolve-toctou-001","type":"pattern","fact":"Tmux Attach mode resolves <session>:<window> to a stable @<window_id> ONCE at construction via 'tmux display-message -p ... #{window_id}'; validates against ^@[0-9]+$. The pinned ID is stored and used for attach. Names are NOT re-resolved per call. Defends against a window being destroyed and re-created with the same name by a different owner mid-conversation.","recommendation":"Whenever you bind to a named tmux target (window, pane, session) for a multi-call interaction, capture the @-prefixed numeric ID at construction and use that. Validate the regex; reject hostile injection (anything not ^@[0-9]+$). Optionally re-probe on every recv (gated by a flag) to detect mid-session destruction.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"WU10 implementation + DoD #21","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["tmux","toctou","security","backend"],"affectedFiles":["src/PureClaw/Backend/Tmux.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-hsboot-redact-cycle-001","type":"pattern","fact":"PureClaw.Handles.Backend needs hand-written Show instances that delegate to PureClaw.Internal.Redact, but Internal.Redact also imports Handles.Backend's error types. Resolved with Internal/Redact.hs-boot exporting only the minimal interface (redactedShowString, credentialPromptScrubber). Handles.Backend imports the .hs-boot under {-# SOURCE #-}.","recommendation":"When a module pair has a Show-instance-vs-error-types cycle, create an .hs-boot for the redactor that exports only the helpers the upstream needs. Do NOT export the full redactor surface from the .hs-boot — keep it minimal so future regressions don't drift the cycle wider.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"WU2 cycle-breaking","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["haskell","module-cycle","hs-boot","redaction"],"affectedFiles":["src/PureClaw/Internal/Redact.hs-boot","src/PureClaw/Internal/Redact.hs","src/PureClaw/Handles/Backend.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-allowlist-warning-split-001","type":"pattern","fact":"Allow-list open-warning code is split to keep Core.Types IO-free: pure helpers (allowListOpen, allowListWarning) and the AllowListContext record {_alc_channelName, _alc_configTable, _alc_exampleId} live in Core.Types; the IO shim (emitAllowListWarning Handle->LogHandle->...; warnIfOpenAllowList = emitAllowListWarning stdout) lives in Channels.AllowList. Banner->stdout (matches the PureClaw 0.1.0 startup banner); WARN->stderr. AllowListContext carries the lowercase TOML table key separately from the display name so config examples render [signal] not [Signal]. emitAllowListWarning takes an injectable Handle for temp-file test capture (no System.IO.Silently dep).","recommendation":"Reuse warnIfOpenAllowList + an AllowListContext for any new channel open-list warning; keep pure rendering in Core.Types and IO in Channels.AllowList.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"PR #73","date":"2026-05-31"}],"tags":["pattern","channels","testing"],"affectedFiles":["src/PureClaw/Channels/AllowList.hs","src/PureClaw/Core/Types.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-31T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-31T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id": "pattern-cover-broker-publish-arm-001", "type": "pattern", "fact": "To unit-test a Frontend.API broker-publish arm (the Just broker branch), build a Just-broker FrontendEnv (mkInProcessBroker defaultBrokerConfig), _streamBroker_subscribe, exercise the endpoint, then drain the subscription queue and filter for the expected BrokerEvent (e.g. ActivityChanged _ (SaSessionCreated m)). See ActivityProbeSpec D18 + APISpec WU4 broker-publish test.", "recommendation": "Don't leave broker-publish arms uncovered with a Nothing broker; the capture harness already exists and pins both the publish AND the payload (e.g. that post-spawn meta carries the real TbTmux backend).", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-99a / adversarial review", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["testing", "broker", "coverage", "frontend"], "affectedFiles": ["test/Frontend/APISpec.hs", "test/Frontend/ActivityProbeSpec.hs"], "affectedServices": ["StreamBroker"], "createdAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "pattern-tmux-authorize-seam-001", "type": "pattern", "fact": "Every tmux subprocess call routes through ONE chokepoint `tmuxProc :: AuthorizedCommand -> ProcessConfig` built only from an AuthorizedCommand minted by the manager-owned `authorizeTmuxCommand` (reuses Security.Command.AuthorizedCommand whose value ctor is unexported). Bare `P.proc tmux` appears nowhere else, so an unauthorized tmux call is impossible by construction.", "recommendation": "For a manager-owned external tool, add a dedicated always-permitted-but-logged constructor on the existing AuthorizedCommand type (don't invent a new policy type) and funnel all spawns through a single ProcessConfig builder; prove the seam with a grep for bare P.proc.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 1)", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["tmux", "security", "authorization", "seam"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Security/Command.hs", "src/PureClaw/Harness/Tmux.hs"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "pattern-honest-staged-coverage-waiver-001", "type": "pattern", "fact": "Per-WU coverage is a BINDING VALIDATE gate (.coverage-thresholds.json blockTaskCompletion=true, 95%). Real-tmux/IO integration-only code is handled with an HONEST stagedWaivers entry (stagedBy/filledBy/since/reason/minimalChecks) whose waived scope is ONLY the untestable IO \u2014 ALL pure logic must actually be covered; cheaply-testable helpers are tested, not waived.", "recommendation": "When a new module mixes pure logic with untestable IO, cover all pure logic first, then add a scoped staged waiver naming exactly the IO functions and enumerating the pure assertions that DID land (minimalChecks). Final review must verify every waiver is honest and has a filledBy follow-up.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 1)", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["coverage", "testing", "waiver", "process"], "affectedFiles": [".coverage-thresholds.json"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "security-pcl-id-pid-corroboration-001", "type": "security", "fact": "A tmux harness window is treated as 'ours' only when its @pcl_id user-option marker AND a recorded shell/harness PID match (a PID-only/no-marker match needs a second signal: pane_start_time or window-name prefix). This \u00a78 C4 corroboration is enforced SYMMETRICALLY: the reconcile sweep never captures/marks-live an uncorroborated window, and routing (isPidCorroborated) refuses to send keystrokes to one. harnessPidOf descends from pane_pid (never a global grep) with a visited-set cycle guard.", "recommendation": "Defend marker spoofing AND PID reuse by requiring marker+PID corroboration on BOTH the discovery/health side and the send/routing side; fail closed (never route to an uncorroborated entry). Derive descendant PIDs by bounded descent from the known pane pid, not a global process scan.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 1)", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["security", "harness", "tmux", "identity", "corroboration"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Harness/Reconcile.hs", "src/PureClaw/Harness/Tmux.hs", "src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs"], "affectedServices": ["HarnessRegistry"], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "pattern-index-action-shared-sort-001", "type": "pattern", "fact": "Frontend per-row actions (Dismiss/Acknowledge) send a display tab INDEX; the backend must resolve that index against the SAME deterministic sort that produced GET /api/tabs (a shared sortedHarnessEntries used by both harnessEntriesToTabs and tabIndexToEntry). A divergent sort would make an action hit the wrong row.", "recommendation": "When an action endpoint is keyed by a list index, share the exact ordering function between the list endpoint and the action resolver (one sort, one snapshot) so index N names the same row on both sides; assert it with an ordering test.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 2)", "date": "2026-06-02"}], "tags": ["frontend", "api", "harness", "routing", "ordering"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T17:06:30.577980+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T17:06:30.577980+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
